# DbAccounts — project knowledge

Cross-platform **PostgreSQL role maintenance** desktop app: manage clusters, batch-run role operations via **user-defined PostgreSQL functions** (not direct DDL in app).

## Product decisions (do not regress)

| Topic | Decision |
|-------|----------|
| UI shell | **Wails v2** + embedded WebView; frontend is vanilla HTML/CSS/JS in `frontend/` |
| DB driver | **pgx/v5**; direct **TCP** to `host:port` (no SSH tunnels in v1) |
| Secrets | **Never** store passwords in YAML; optional `connect_user` only. No in-UI credential fields. Auth: user = cluster `connect_user` → `PGUSER`; password = `PGPASSWORD` → `~/.pgpass` → **empty** (trust / no password, like psql). Production gated by a confirm popup (no checkbox). |
| Role logic | App calls **call templates** with `${placeholder}` → `SELECT fn($1,...)` — real DDL/privileges live in **DB functions** on each cluster |
| Categories | = cluster groups. Editable in Settings (label + base `color` + `confirm` flag); id is a slug of the label. Colours applied via a generated `<style id="cat-colors">` keyed on `data-cat` (no hardcoded prod/uat colours). `confirm` drives the production popup. |
| DB function specs | User will provide real names/signatures; defaults in `config.example.yaml` are placeholders (`your_schema.*`) |

## Stack (current)

- Go module: `github.com/michalbartak/dbaccounts`
- Wails **v2.12.0** (CLI may auto-bump `go.mod` on `wails dev`)
- pgx v5, yaml.v3, google/uuid
- Bindings: `frontend/wailsjs/` — **auto-generated** by Wails; do not hand-edit; regenerate via `wails dev` / `wails build`

## Config file

| OS | Path |
|----|------|
| macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/DbAccounts/config.yaml` |
| Linux | `~/.config/dbaccounts/config.yaml` |
| Windows | `%AppData%\DbAccounts\config.yaml` |

Example template: [`config.example.yaml`](config.example.yaml). Implemented in `internal/config/` (`paths.go`, `store.go`).

**YAML keys:** `version`, `categories`, `clusters`, `db_functions.<op>.call`, `db_functions.<op>.execution`, `batch.max_concurrency` (default 5), `ui.theme`, `parent_roles` (preconfigured parent groups — bare identifiers, offered as pick-list choices when granting privileges; Create-role `parent_role` accepts a comma-separated list). Legacy `name`/`params` migrated on load.

## Wails API (`app.go` → `window.go.main.App`)

- `GetConfig`, `GetConfigPath`, `ReloadConfig`, `GetAppVersion`
- `AddCluster`, `UpdateCluster`, `DeleteCluster` (per-item; kept but unused by the UI now)
- `SaveClusters(ClustersConfig)` — staged Clusters editor: replaces the whole clusters+categories
  set atomically via `Store.SaveClustersAndCategories` (validate + UUID/slug ids + referential integrity)
- `ImportFromEnvironment` — reads `PGHOST`, `PGPORT`, `PGDATABASE`, `PGUSER`
- `SaveDBFunctions`, `SaveBatchSettings`, `SaveUISettings`, `SaveParentRoles`, `SaveTargetSelection`
- `TestConnection`, `PreviewTargets`, `RunRoleBatch` (per-cluster transactional batch — the
  create/update/remove path), `RunOperation` (legacy single-op, unused by the UI)
- **Introspection (reads, for Alter role):** `SearchRoles`, `LoadRoleDetails` — scan the
  **selected** clusters concurrently (`internal/pg/introspect.go` + `batch.Runner`),
  collecting per-cluster errors instead of failing. The three read queries are **templatable**
  (`Config.DBReads`, YAML `db_reads.<search_roles|role_detail|role_parents>.query`; vanilla
  catalog defaults + migrate/validate in `internal/config/dbreads.go`). `batch.Runner` passes
  each query into `pg` (which stays config-free); each takes one named `${rolename}` bind (rewritten
  to `$1` before Query; legacy `$1` still works) and its result columns
  are scanned **by name** via `pgx.RowToStructByNameLax` (order-independent; NULL comment/rolconfig
  OK; omitted contract column → zero; **extra** column → error). Contracts: search_roles →
  `rolname, comment`; role_detail → 7 `rol*` bools + `comment` + `rolconfig`; role_parents →
  `rolname`. Editable in Settings → **Introspection queries** (`#fn-dialog` read mode; Default
  button reverts). Bound method `SaveDBReads`. Override a read with a privileged wrapper
  function/view that returns the contract columns.

## Call templates (`internal/calltemplate/`)

Config: `db_functions.<operation>.call` + optional `.execution` (`function` \| `statement` \| `block`). Docs: [`sql/README.md`](sql/README.md).

| `operation` | Allowed `${...}` | Notes |
|-------------|------------------|-------|
| `create_role` | loginname, fullname, email, parent_role | `ARRAY \|\|` requires `execution: function` |
| `remove_role` | loginname, rolename (alias) | `statement`: e.g. `DROP ROLE ${loginname}`; `block`: a complete anonymous block (`DO $tag$ … $tag$;`), run verbatim |
| `grant_parents` | loginname, parent_roles | `statement`: `GRANT ${parent_roles} TO ${loginname}` — identifiers, not quoted |
| `revoke_parents` | loginname, parent_roles | Default `statement`: `REVOKE ${parent_roles} FROM ${loginname}` |
| `change_password` | loginname, new_password | |
| `set_comment` | loginname, comment | Default `statement`: `COMMENT ON ROLE ${loginname} IS ${comment}` — comment as escaped literal |
| `set_attribute` | loginname, attributes (alias: attribute) | Default `statement`: `ALTER ROLE ${loginname} WITH ${attributes}` — space-separated whitelisted keywords (SUPERUSER/NOSUPERUSER/…), embedded unquoted |
| `set_config` | loginname, config_name, config_value | Default `statement`: `ALTER ROLE ${loginname} SET ${config_name} = ${config_value}` — `config_name` is a bare unquoted GUC name (`fieldConfigName`, `gucNameRE`-validated), value a literal. Role GUCs read from `pg_roles.rolconfig`. |
| `reset_config` | loginname, config_name | Default `statement`: `ALTER ROLE ${loginname} RESET ${config_name}` |

**Execution:** `function` → `SELECT` + `$n` binds (`Query`). `statement` / `block` → embed values (`Exec`): role fields as identifiers (`loginname`, `parent_roles` list on grant_parents); passwords/names as quoted literals. Do not use raw `$1` in templates.

**Defaults are vanilla PostgreSQL DDL (statement mode)** — e.g. create_role default:

`CREATE ROLE ${loginname}`

(fullname/email/parent_role are unused by the vanilla default; a `function`-mode override can
consume them, e.g. `admin_access.create_role(${loginname}, NULL, ${fullname}, ${email}, ARRAY['grp'] || ${parent_role})`).
Loading an existing config never force-overwrites user templates; the `#fn-dialog` **Default**
button reverts one template to the vanilla built-in.

**Template processing:**

- **Function mode:** `${field}` → `$n` text bind from form (`internal/commands` arg map).
- **Statement/block:** `loginname`, `parent_roles`, `parent_role`, `rolename` → unquoted identifiers; `parent_roles` split on commas (grant/revoke); `new_password`, `fullname`, `email` → SQL string literals.
- `ARRAY['a','b'] || ${field}` → fixed array literal + `|| NULL` if field empty, else `|| $n::text[]` with `[]string{value}` (processed before other placeholders).
- `ARRAY[${field}, 'a', 'b']` → normalized to `ARRAY['a','b'] || ${field}` via `normalizeTemplate`.
- Reject `${Array...}`, `SELECT`, `;`. Legacy `${array_concat:...}` still parsed; migrate broken configs in `internal/config/dbfunctions.go`.

`internal/pg/function.go` → `calltemplate.Build` + `Query` (function) or `Exec` (statement/block).

## UI (`frontend/`)

Tabs: **Operations**, **Clusters**, **Settings**, with **Create role** + **Alter role**
op-tabs right-aligned in the same bar (visible only while Operations is active). Prod/UAT
badges in CSS. Per-cluster outcomes render in the **Status** panel (hidden until
non-empty). Do not add a heavy frontend framework unless requested.

**App-shell layout:** `body` is a flex column with `overflow:hidden` (no whole-page
scroll); header + tabs fixed. Operations = two independently scrolling columns
(`.ops-sidebar` / `.ops-main`); `.ops-main` has a scrolling `.ops-body` + pinned
`.ops-footer` (Run or Save/Remove, via `updateOpsFooter()`). Clusters/Settings are
single-column, sharing a padded panel + inset **`[Discard] [Save]`** footer (Settings:
`btn-discard-settings`/`btn-save-settings`+`discardSettings`; the divider goes up to the content
margins, not the window). The **Clusters tab is STAGED**
like Settings: cluster/group add/edit/delete mutate `clustersDraft`/`categoriesDraft` (seeded
once from saved `state` in `loadConfig`); nothing persists until the pinned **Save**/**Discard**
footer (`btn-save-clusters` → `App.SaveClusters` → `Store.SaveClustersAndCategories`, atomic
validate+replace; Save enabled-when-dirty / disabled-when-clean via `clustersDirty`). Only the Clusters editor
reads the drafts — Operations keeps reading saved `state`. **Test connections**
(`btn-test-clusters` → `testAllClusters`) tests the on-screen **draft** values via
`TestConnectionInput` into a per-row **Status** column (`setClusterStatus`). Left sidebar is Target selection only; "Or pick clusters" collapses/expands
(collapsed by default; expanded list flexes to fill). Target selection is **remembered**
(module-level `selectedCategoryIds`=null→all / `selectedClusterIds`, seeded once from
persisted `Config.Targets`, re-render keeps it, persisted via `SaveTargetSelection`) so it
survives Settings-save and restarts. **Cluster groups** are edited from
the Clusters toolbar (right-aligned `btn-manage-groups` → `#groups-dialog` list →
`#group-dialog` form; no Save button, so not in Settings). Feature descriptions live
behind a **`?` help badge** (`.q-hint`, via `hintBadge(text)`); mouse hover shows a shared
`position:fixed`, viewport-clamped popover (`.q-hint-pop`) driven by delegated
`mouseover`/`keydown` handlers (no forced `tabindex`; opens on Enter/Space when
keyboard-focused, not on plain focus).

**Shared UI conventions (solve once, don't re-patch per popup):** open every `<dialog>` via
the `openModal(dlgOrId)` helper (never bare `.showModal()`) — it drops `showModal()`'s
auto-focus ring on the first Close/OK button unless the dialog has an `[autofocus]` element.
Focus indicators are keyboard-only (`:focus-visible`) and **inset** (border + `inset`
box-shadow; light ring on primary-filled controls) so scroll/`overflow:hidden` containers
can't clip them — one `styles.css` rule for text fields/buttons/checkboxes. Base `dialog` is
`padding:0`; each `*-dialog-body` sets its own padding. Header `.brand` row (dot + smaller
title + version chip + `ⓘ #btn-about`) opens `#about-dialog` (`GetAppVersion`;
`runtime.BrowserOpenURL` links).

**Alter role** (search-then-edit): clicking the **Alter role** op-tab opens a search
dialog (no separate "Find user" button) that searches the *selected*
clusters (name + `COMMENT ON ROLE`), grouped by login; picking one opens a single
consolidated form. Privileges (`pg_auth_members`) and attributes (superuser, createrole,
createdb, inherit, login, replication, bypassrls) list one-per-row with **scope labels**
judged per group (outlined/bordered group label when all selected clusters of a group match
— matching Target selection's group boxes — else filled per-cluster labels; coloured by
environment). **✎ Edit** opens a per-cluster
checkbox editor that grants **and** revokes; **×** removes everywhere; **↺** discards
pending. **Settings** (role GUCs) use the same editor keyed by `name=value`
(`alterConfigSet`/`alterConfigReset`), emitting `set_config`/`reset_config`. Comments
popup groups clusters by comment content (compared as JSON by value) and saves via
`set_comment`. Edit state: `alterAdd`/`alterRevoke`, `alterAttrAdd`/`alterAttrRemove` are
`Map<key, Set<clusterId>>`; `describeScope` / `scopeLabelsHtml` produce all labels.

**Create and Alter share one `#role-form`** rendered by `renderAlterDetail` over
`alterDetails` + the `alter*` edit maps. Mode = `isCreateMode()` (`currentOp`). Create =
editing a not-yet-existing role with an empty synthetic baseline (`synthCreateBaseline()`
from `resolveSelectedClusters()`; `reconcilePendingWithUniverse()` on selection change);
Alter = search → `pickUser` → `reloadDetails`. The static `#role-identity` block holds login
(readonly in edit) + an inline **comment editor** (`#role-comment-editor`, module-level
`commentEditor` state, `loadCommentEditor`). Comments are **format-agnostic** (plain text or
arbitrary JSON, no forced keys): Fields↔Raw toggle, Fields edits string values only, labels
come from Settings-managed `Config.CommentFields` (`comment_fields`, default full_name/e_mail,
`SaveCommentFields`); empty comments default to `ui.comment_default_view` (`preferredCommentView`);
`editorFromComment`/`assembleComment(From)`/`switchEditorMode`/`parseCommentObject` are the core
helpers. Run: both modes build per-cluster ordered op lists and send ONE
`App.RunRoleBatch(RoleBatchRequest)` (`executeRoleBatch`); the backend (`batch.runClusterTx`) runs
each cluster's ops in a **single transaction** (commit/rollback, one result per cluster, bounded
concurrency), emitting a `role-batch-progress` Wails event (`model.ClusterProgress`) per cluster
start/finish so the UI shows live progress in the footer status chip `#run-status` (button-sized,
neutral color, spinner-only-while-running, no ✓/✕ glyph) (+ its `#run-status-dialog` popup — no
Host column; each done row has a magnifier (`.rst-view`) opening a larger `#run-queries-dialog`
with that cluster's executed SQL — not shown inline — plus a copy button that copies message +
all queries). Each `ClusterResult`/`ClusterProgress` carries `Queries []string` (executed SQL from
`pg.ExecuteOperation`'s `(sql, msg, err)` return; function-mode binds inlined; failing op's SQL
kept). `clearRunStatus()` clears it on op-tab/page-tab switch so it never leaks across pages.
**No corner toast** (`showToast` removed): simple confirmations flash the action button
("Saved"/"Created", `flashButton`); Save buttons are enabled-when-dirty / disabled-when-clean,
no marker (`setDirty` toggles `disabled`; disabled = `pointer-events:none`, no hover — Settings
`settingsDirty`, role `buildAlterClusterOps().length>0`, Clusters `clustersDirty`). All
right-aligned action buttons + op-tabs align to the 1.25rem panel edge. Errors/validation render
inline in a `.form-error` (`showInlineError` →
`#ops-error`/`#settings-error`/`#clusters-error`/`#scope-error`/`#group-error`/
`#cluster-test-error`/`#alter-search-errors`) + a red button flash; run outcomes stay in the chip.
`buildAlterClusterOps` orders grant→revoke→password→**set_attribute (all keywords
combined)**→set_config→reset_config→set_comment; create prepends `create_role`
(`buildCreateClusterOps`). Comment persists via `set_comment` (per-cluster `commentOverrides` wins,
else `assembleComment`; create's `create_role` gets `${fullname}`/`${email}` from the editor,
follow-up `set_comment` authoritative). When comments vary the inline editor hides and the Comments
dialog reconciles per cluster (`commentVersionEditors`). One shared
`confirmScopeDialog`/`buildScopeTargets` (no create fork). **Errors never touch the role form**:
`executeRoleBatch` returns the results array or `null`; on `null`/any per-cluster failure the
Save/Create/Remove paths leave the form + pending edits intact (chip/popup are the only error
surface). Only a fully clean run refreshes the form — Save re-reads via `fetchRoleDetails` and
re-renders only when that reload is itself clean (never clobbers on transient unreachable); the
"not found" empty state still renders for a real search `pickUser`.

## Versioning & packaging

- App semver: [`VERSION`](VERSION) — git tags `v$(cat VERSION)` (see [`RELEASING.md`](RELEASING.md)).
- `make sync-wails-version` updates `wails.json` `productVersion`.
- `make package` — `wails build` with `-ldflags` (version/commit/date) + `dist/` archive.
- UI: `GetAppVersion()`; config YAML `version:` is **schema** version only.

